    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d98-a2">

                <pb facs="0227" n="187" sameAs="frus:frus1865p1/pg187"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure No. 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Nesbet to Mr.
                        Kirkpatrick.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colonial Secretary’s Office</hi>. <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Nassau,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-01-31"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 31, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am directed by the governor to
                    acknowledge the receipt of your letter of yesterday enclosing a newspaper
                    referring to the character of the steamer Rattlesnake, which has recently
                    entered this harbor, and to Inform you that there is nothing in your letter or
                    its en” closure which appears to his excellency to create a suspicion against it
                    greater than that which attaches to every vessel of the same class with which
                    this harbor is filled, or to call for any action on the part of the government
                    beyond that of vigilance, which is already exercised with regard to all vessels
                    engaged in trade with the southern States.</p>
                <p>I have the Honor to be, sir, your most obedient and humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C. R. NESBET, <hi rendition="#italic">Colonial
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thomas Kirkpatrick</hi>. Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Consul, Nassau.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
